   "evidence": "HalfLine.lean:42-56 \u2014 the proof body mentions `^ 2` only inside the `EqOn` statements it carries along; `Set.apply_piecewise` exists at upstream/mathlib/Mathlib/Data/Set/Piecewise.lean:129 (`h x (s.piecewise f g x) = s.piecewise (fun x => h x (f x)) (fun x => h x (g x)) x`). Both uses of the lemma in the PR are squares, so the corollary keeps every call site as is.",
   "file": "EpsilonEridani/Mathematics/MeasureTheory/HalfLine.lean",
   "fix": "State the general lemma `theorem setIntegral_piecewise_Ioi_const {b R : \u211d} (hbR : b \u2264 R) (a : E) {f : \u211d \u2192 E} (hf : IntegrableOn f (Ioi R)) : \u222b r in Ioi b, (Ioi R).piecewise f (fun _ => a) r = (R - b) \u2022 a + \u222b r in Ioi R, f r` with the identical proof, and keep the `_sq` form as a one-line corollary: `Set.apply_piecewise` (Mathlib/Data/Set/Piecewise.lean:129) rewrites `(Ioi R).piecewise v (fun _ => a) r ^ 2` as `(Ioi R).piecewise (fun r => v r ^ 2) (fun _ => a ^ 2) r`, so the two call sites (`glued` at DeuteronWave.lean:363-364 and `dStateProbability_glued` at line 381) are unchanged.",
   "issue": "`setIntegral_piecewise_Ioi_const_sq` is restricted to `v r ^ 2` with a real `a ^ 2`, but the proof (EqOn on `Ioc b R` and on `Ioi R`, then `setIntegral_union` + `setIntegral_const`) never uses the square; the squaring is baked into a lemma in a subject-independent `Mathematics/MeasureTheory` file, so the next caller needing the un-squared integral must re-prove it. The sibling `memLp_piecewise_Ioi_const` (line 32) in the same file is stated for general `E` and `p`, so the file is inconsistent about its own level.",
   "line": "42"
  }
 ],
